Z||000000||FieroKyle||08-25-2001||10:10 PM||||Alright, I am not a great drag guy but uh I am not terrible.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif">, Uh when I do a 1/4 mile run when I can find a piece of smooth flat pavement out here in the country (a rarity in Michigan). I will get my stop watch out and time me. My fastest 1/4 mile has been 15.8 and 0 to 60 in 8.5. Alls I am doing is letting of the gas and pushing the cluth in and shifting as fast I can. My dad says you can speed shift using the clutch never letting off the gas and shifting quick enough before you blow the engine. I don't dare to try it just cuz the fear of wrecking the motor. So is my way pretty much the best way and fastest way to shift on just a stock 85' GT with the 4-speed and doing is safely? The car has 116K on it so its getting up there in miles. MAy be what I am asking is how or what is fastest way to shift, this may be hard to explain with a first hand expierence and practice on a drag strip. I am just asking may be a explanation from the guys do drag race. Another side note is when I have race people at stop lights that have automatic transmission, I seem to lose about 3 to 4 feet in ground everytime I shift even if I red line and shift as quick as I can.||||reg||1
Z||000001||DRH||08-25-2001||11:21 PM||||Speed shifting is rough on your tranny (especially the syncronizers) and the clutch too. Over reving can happen, but is not as much of a problem since the ECM shuts off fuel just above redline. Speed shifting should give you slightly faster times, but your car will definitely live longer the way you're doing it now.<P><BR>||||reg||1
